  "slug": "optimal-transport-flow-matching-ea35",
  "summary": "Preprints test protein and single-cell foundation models for leakage, baseline parity and error control, plus recalibrated pathway and kinase inference.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is stricter evaluation and statistical calibration of computational predictors rather than new architectures. Protify standardizes protein language model benchmarking across zero-shot, supervised and transfer settings and reports task dependence and homology leakage. PPI-Caliper applies conformal calibration to protein language model interaction scores, controlling false discovery rate without retraining across five species. A single-cell benchmark compares five foundation models with simple baselines for annotation, in silico perturbation and GRN inference and finds that the foundation models help only in some settings. The same concern with calibration appears outside foundation models. ssGSEA3.0 replaces feature-label permutation with feature-level bootstrap resampling to improve significance calibration. A kinase activity study benchmarks Kinase Library-expanded priors on 222 phosphoproteomic samples. Two further preprints, ExPert for causal perturbation inference and Borzoi fine-tuned on synthetic MPRA labels, extend model capabilities rather than evaluation. What is new is the use of leakage-aware protocols, baseline comparisons and formal error control as the standard for judging model claims.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-09"
}
